{
  "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
  "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "David L. McColgin (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "FBI agents delayed presenting Mr. Corley to a Federal magistrate judge in order to obtain his two confessions. The admissibility of these two confessions depends on an issue of statutory interpretation: The interpretation of 3501(c), together with the McNabb-Mallory rule and the right of prompt presentment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you arguing that the language in subsection (c) codifies the McNabb-Mallory rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David L. McColgin (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It leaves McNabb-Mallory in place. However, the language of the statute uses the phrase \"time limitation\" in the proviso. \"Time limitation\" implies more than we're just not just touching McNabb-Mallory for the time being. It depends -- the statute depends on McNabb-Mallory to create the time limitation, because without McNabb-Mallory there is no limitation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, is it your position that the McNabb-Mallory rule serves purposes other than to ensure the voluntariness of the statement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, that certainly is a very back-door way of doing it, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But why -- why was it appropriate to have a special rule for transportation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that enough of a disincentive? If you delay too long, that delay is one of the factors to be taken into account in deciding whether the confession was voluntary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "only provide punishment for excessive delay where there has been a confession. Isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that is the answer, why do we need (c) -- I mean, why did Congress need (c) at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why should we interpret (a) as setting those other things aside and requiring us to overturn McNabb and Mallory?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you familiar with cases in which a defendant's confession has been excluded under -- under 403?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think in theory Rule 403 is such a rule. Rule 16, which requires discovery obligations, contains its own authorization for an exclusionary rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Then why didn't the statute say, instead of saying inadmissible, shall not be found involuntary solely by reasons of delay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is, and I think the reason that it was written that way, Justice Souter, is it was a direct attempt to make clear that McNabb-Mallory shall not operate in the six-hour period after arrests and before presentment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ad4c562a05d7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where we have such purposeful delay, Congress left McNabb-Mallory in place to address precisely such flagrant conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-10441",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "ad4c562a05d7e3e85d7f349004ca987144b7bdc2996231dc7a0b9c991ce10e6e",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-ad4c562a05d7-52",
